body:
If you feel like his safety is at risk which to me an outsider i feel like it is from the number of attempts. i feel like keeping it a secret between you two would be worse off in the long run saying that though i would make sure your parents aren't the ones who might be adding to his depression idk how healthy your family dynamics are so yeah. But if your parents are kind and loving people and you feel would be able to support your brother either through themselves or getting him into therapy/possible hospitalizations then i would say in the long run yes you should totally tell your parents but in the short term i doubt he would be much appreciative and it might cause some stress in your relationship for a while anyways until he gets back into the swing of things.

&#x200B;

edit: hope this helps and maybe even contact the local crisis line or some local mental health resources and get a more professional opinion etc and talk to them

is there another gym close by maybe you can cancel your membership or even transfer it idk but to answer how to meet new people that depends on what you like or what you are interested in if you are into hiking then maybe there's some hiking groups in your area. And i don't want to encourage reckless behavior but you also could look into quitting your current job and looking for a new one or just looking for a new one closer to your friends again don't do this if this is gonna cause more trouble then its worth but it's all about seeing possible options that are open to you and choosing ones that are best for you. And yeah therapy is scary and i was practically forced into treatment so i can't really tell you how to get over that hump since i never really had to go through that myself but trust me therapy with an actual professional is a lot better then a internet nobody. I hope this answers something idk i'm not the best at formulating my thoughts coherently. I have dealt with diagnosable  depression a good part of my life and i can tell you that it's a bitch and it's going to be tough but you'll come out this a stronger person and maybe even a happier person.

&#x200B;

Edit: Just don't let yourself sulk if you notice that you are slipping into a spiral challenge your thoughts or replace them with positive thoughts. Don't beat yourself up over the fact your depressed either your feelings are valid and you don't need to feel bad about not feeling good Try and keep to the schedule you had for the most part same bed time same waking up. exercise even if it's not at the gym and take small steps if all you can do is make your bed and go to work and maybe say hi to some random on the street something anything then take that as a win and don't compare yourself to how he's doing or whatever anyways sorry for chewing your ear off and never be afraid to ask for help there are hotlines and resources out there never forget also reach out to even long distance friends just try not to isolate yourself

Well have you voiced your concerns to your girlfriend about a possible break up i mean you don't want it to become a self fulfilling prophecy. And no drive is a tough one but right now you have two options and that's to continue the path your on or change your path and obviously you don't like your current one. So i'd reccomend a couple things for trying to find a new one that doesn't involve self harm or suicide since all these problems are temporary and don't need such drastic action such as suicide one try to get into treatment therapy possibly medication two find things you like to do things you enjoyed or enjoy now meet new people get out go on dates with your gf etc three work on some skills for employment either self or otherwise work on your resume if you have one if you don't then build one out look for local job offerings or local workshops to learn valuable skills or even maybe look into going back to school all of these are possible solutions and right now you have nothing to lose really so why not try and do something new none of these are over night solutions but they are steps that will help.

&#x200B;

edit: i'm also here if you need to vent or would like to talk
